<article class="env-lemma" id="03L8">
  <p><a class="environment-identifier" href="/tag/03L8">Lemma <span data-tag="03L8">34.9.5</span>.</a> Let $T$ be a scheme. Let $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ be a family of morphisms of schemes with target $T$. Assume that </p>
  <p><ol>
  <li><p>
each $f_ i$ is flat, and 
</p>
</li><li><p>
the family $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ can be refined by an fpqc covering of $T$. 
</p>
</li>
</ol></p>
  <p> Then $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ is an fpqc covering of $T$. </p>
</article><article class="env-proof">
    <p>
      <strong>Proof.</strong>
      Let $\{ g_ j : X_ j \to T\} _{j \in J}$ be an fpqc covering refining $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} $. Suppose that $U \subset T$ is affine open. Choose $j_1, \ldots , j_ m \in J$ and $V_ k \subset X_{j_ k}$ affine open such that $U = \bigcup g_{j_ k}(V_ k)$. For each $j$ pick $i_ j \in I$ and a morphism $h_ j : X_ j \to T_{i_ j}$ such that $g_ j = f_{i_ j} \circ h_ j$. Since $h_{j_ k}(V_ k)$ is quasi-compact we can find a quasi-compact open $h_{j_ k}(V_ k) \subset U_ k \subset f_{i_{j_ k}}^{-1}(U)$. Then $U = \bigcup f_{i_{j_ k}}(U_ k)$. We conclude that $\{ f_ i : T_ i \to T\} _{i \in I}$ is an fpqc covering by Lemma <a href="/tag/03L7" data-tag="03L7">34.9.2</a>. 
      <span class="qed">$\square$</span>
    </p>
</article>